{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791122735,"nonce":"NmvpQzxPRlYMQ9THmt9A0sIVxOM=","title":"A tier promotion of a large shared bundle holds about 200MB of native memory while it compiles","message":"An idle ashui window (no frames drawn, GC heap 3.3MB live) climbs from 128MB RSS to a 327MB peak during one tier promotion, then falls back to 129MB once it completes. The user saw \"ash using up to 500mb\" in windowed ashui scenes.\n\nFrom an ashui checkout beside ash, hlwgpu and hlwindow (built):\n\n    ASHUI_WINDOW_SECONDS=55 ASH_AIR_LOG=1 tools/snapshot/run.sh --window tools/snapshot/scenes/CanvasGallery.hx\n\nSample RSS each second with `ps -axo rss,command | grep CanvasGallery.hl`.\n\n- 5-8s: startup compile, RSS up to 251MB, back to 128MB by 21s.\n- 27s: with the window idle (2 frames drawn in total, main thread 95% in mach_msg2_trap), RSS climbs to 327MB over 27-39s.\n- 39s: `[promote] findex=448 path=shared bodies=437 middle_end=1787ms`.\n- 40-48s: RSS drains to 129MB and stays there.\n- ASH_GC_STATS: 1 collection, 3.3MB live. The growth is native: the profiler's non-main samples are in air::v2 passes (sroa::classify, licm, write_class, gvn, liveness).\n- Control, the Demo scene (no canvas): no promotion, flat at about 126MB.\n\n- About 200MB transient for a 437-body middle end looks high: per-body IR kept alive across the whole bundle? Cloned instruction vectors (`Instr::clone` shows in the samples)?\n- Why does an idle program promote at 27s? Time-based tiering of what ran at startup?\n\nReported from ashui (session ashui-10).","files":null}]}